 To implement the Sobel edge detection algorithm with a Gaussian filter in MATLAB, you can follow these steps:
1. Read the input image and convert it to grayscale.
2. Apply a Gaussian filter to reduce the noise in the image.
3. Define the Sobel operators in x and y directions.
4. Apply the Sobel operators to the filtered image.
5. Combine the edges in both directions.
6. Threshold the edge image to get binary edges.
7. Display the resulting edge image.
Here's the modified code:
```matlab
% Read input image and convert to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter to reduce noise
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3,3], 1.5); % Standard deviation of 1.5
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter, 'same');
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operators to the filtered image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Threshold the edge image to get binary edges
threshold_value = 0.05 * max(max(edge_image(:))); % Set threshold based on maximum value in edge image
binary_edges = (edge_image > threshold_value) * 255;
% Display original image, edge image, and binary edges
figure;
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');

